Terms and Conditions of Access</h3><h4>1. Definitions</h4><p> &quot;Database&quot; means any structured set of data compiled by FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS. The Databases form part of the FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS Content. </p><p> &quot;CV Database&quot; means the database of Candidate profiles and CVs to which the Services give access. The CV Database forms part of the Databases. </p><p>&quot;Candidate&quot; means a member registered on the free-work.com website.</p><p> &quot;Recruitment Agency Customer&quot; means Customers subscribing to an access plan whose business consists in handling all or part of their own clients&#39; recruitment processes. </p><p> &quot;Content&quot; means all data, information, documents, files, texts, images, videos, audio or audiovisual recordings, graphics, metadata, databases, templates, forms, questionnaires, reports, analyses, recommendations, best practices, methodologies, processes, source code, object and executable code, documentation, preparatory design material, interfaces, logos, drawings and designs to which the Customer may have access in connection with the Services. </p><p> &quot;FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS Content&quot; means the Content owned by or licensed to FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS. </p><p> &quot;Candidate Content&quot; means the Content communicated or published by Candidates. </p><p> &quot;Other Customer and Third-Party Content&quot; means the Content communicated or published by other Customers and by any third parties. </p><h4>2. Purpose</h4><p>These General Terms and Conditions set out:</p><ul><li> the conditions under which FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS provides the Services to the Customer; </li><li> the conditions applicable to the various access plans to which the Customer may subscribe; </li><li>the rules the Customer must comply with when using the Services.</li></ul><h4>3. Services offered</h4><p>Our platform offers, among others, the following Services:</p><ul><li> access to our CV Database made up of Candidates who are members of our free-work.com website; </li><li>the publication of job offers on free-work.com;</li><li> access to our B2B Marketplace, dedicated to the recruitment of consultants between assignments (&quot;intercontrat&quot;), which allows you to access calls for tenders, publish your consultant profiles and establish partnerships; </li><li> recruitment software provided on a SaaS basis (Applicant Tracking System, &quot;ATS&quot;); </li><li> tools to improve and accelerate your recruitment, such as AI matching and tracking tools. </li></ul><p> Some Services may be integrated into the Customer&#39;s system by means of our APIs. </p><p> As part of our continuous improvement policy or for commercial reasons, we reserve the right to modify our Services during the term of the contract, including by adding or removing features. Such changes may not, however, call into question the essential features included in the access plan subscribed to. Any new feature involving the processing of personal data, in particular by means of artificial intelligence, shall be the subject of prior written information to the Customer before it is implemented. </p><h4>4. Subscribing to an access plan</h4><p> 4.1. Eligible persons – Access to our Services is reserved for legal entities duly registered as such and holding a SIRET number (the French business registration number) or an equivalent business registration number in their country of establishment. </p><p> 4.2. Authority – The Customer warrants that the person subscribing is duly authorised to do so. </p><p> 4.3. Selection of the access plan – The Customer selects the access plan that suits it. Before final subscription upon payment, an Order Form setting out the contents of the plan chosen is issued. The Customer may upgrade to a higher plan at any time but has no right to downgrade to a lower plan during the term of the contract. </p><p> 4.4. Customer&#39;s responsibility – It is the Customer&#39;s responsibility, before confirming its order by payment, to satisfy itself that the Services offered meet its needs and that its intended use of the Services complies with our contractual terms and with all applicable regulations. The Services are provided as is. </p><p> 4.5. Final subscription – The subscription is final and irreversible upon receipt of payment by FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS, with no right of withdrawal. Access to the Services will be provided for the term of the access plan subscribed to, with no right of termination before its expiry and no right to a refund on any grounds whatsoever. </p><p> 4.6. Trial – Trial periods are fully subject to these General Terms and Conditions. The trial period runs whether or not the Services are actually used. We may terminate the trial at any time, without having to give any reason. </p><h4>5. Term and financial conditions</h4><h5>5.1. Terms applicable to all access plans</h5><p> 5.1.1. Prices – The prices and rates in force are expressed in euros excluding tax, FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS reserving the right to pass on any new tax or any change to an existing tax. </p><p> Should the Customer be required to make any withholding on its payments, it shall gross up its payments so that FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS receives the net amount that would have been paid to it in the absence of any such withholding. </p><p> 5.1.2. Discounts – FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS may offer discounts for limited periods, without the Customer being entitled to the continuation of such offers. </p><p> 5.1.3. No early-payment rebate – No rebate will be granted for early payment. </p><p> 5.1.4. Price changes – FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS reserves the right to freely modify the prices of its access plans, the Customer having no right to the maintenance of a given price from one subscription to the next. </p><h5>5.2. Fixed-Term Access Plans</h5><p> 5.2.1. Term – Access plans subscribed to for a fixed term are entered into without automatic renewal. The Customer is bound until the expiry date and has no right to a refund or to early termination. </p><p> 5.2.2. Payment and start of access – Payment is made by bank card or bank transfer. Where payment is made by transfer, access starts only upon due receipt of payment and processing of the order by FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS. </p><p> 5.2.3. Pause period – Where the plan subscribed to includes the Pause feature, as indicated on the order form, the Customer has 6 periods of 7 consecutive days (a &quot;Pause Period&quot;) to be spread over the term of the access plan. During these Pause Periods, access is suspended. The expiry date of the access plan is postponed by as many calendar days as access was actually suspended. The Customer may activate a Pause Period at any time on simple request, made no earlier than 12 months before the desired period and no later than the day before (D-1). A Pause Period may start on any day of the week and is counted in calendar days, i.e. including weekends and public holidays. The Customer may interrupt a Pause Period at any time by calling us by telephone. </p><h5>5.3. Monthly START Access Plans</h5><p> 5.3.1. Term and termination – The monthly START access plan gives access to the Services for a period of 30 days (the &quot;Period&quot;), with automatic renewal. The Customer may choose at any time, via our Site, not to renew its access for the following Period. </p><p> 5.3.2. Payment and start of access – Payment is made by bank card only, debited three days before the start of the new Period. Access to the Services starts upon the first payment and is renewed every 30 days thereafter, provided the bank card could be debited prior to the tacit renewal date. </p><p> 5.3.3. Failure to pay – In the absence of payment on the agreed date, access to the Services will be automatically suspended, without prior formal notice or advance warning. To restore access to the Services, the Customer must make the payment due for the forthcoming period. </p><p> 5.3.4. Price changes – Any change in prices will be notified to the Customer with reasonable notice, without prejudice to its right to terminate the tacit renewal of its access plan in the event of disagreement. </p><h4>6. Intellectual property, Data, Confidentiality</h4><p> 6.1. Ownership of FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS Content – FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS owns all rights in the FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS Content or holds the authorisations required for its use. Subject to the rights granted under the licence below, the Contract does not transfer any right in the FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS Content. The Customer shall refrain from any step aimed at having rights in such Content recognised or obtained in its favour, anywhere in the world. </p><p> 6.2. Licence to FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS Content – For the purpose of benefiting from the access plan subscribed to and within the limits set out in the Contract, the Customer is granted the rights to access and use the FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS Content as well as our CV Database. This licence is granted for the term of the Contract and is non-exclusive, non-transferable and non-sublicensable. </p><p> 6.3. Other Content – Candidates, other Customers and any third parties share their content under their own responsibility, in accordance with our Terms of use. </p><p> 6.4. Authorisations granted by the Customer – The Customer grants FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS, for the duration of the Contract, all authorisations necessary for its use of the Services, and in particular the display of its distinctive signs in the spaces provided for that purpose (logos, trade marks, etc.). </p><p> 6.5. Opt-out from text and data mining – FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS objects to all harvesting and text and data mining operations within the meaning of Article L. 122-5-3 of the French Intellectual Property Code. This objection covers the entire Site and all Content to which it gives access. All harvesting and text and data mining operations targeting the Site and the Content, including by means of automated data collection systems, therefore constitute acts of infringement unless a specific agreement has been formally expressed by us. As Article R. 122-28 of the French Intellectual Property Code provides that the objection referred to in III of Article L. 122-5-3 may be expressed by any means, including through the general terms of use of a website or service, the absence of metadata associated with the Site, the Site&#39;s directories or the Site&#39;s Content has no bearing on the exercise of the right of objection expressed in these General terms and Conditions of Access and Use. Texts and data downloaded by means of the APIs are subject to the specific terms set out in the dedicated section. </p><p> 6.6. Confidentiality – Confidential information (hereinafter &quot;Confidential Information&quot;) means all information, data or documents that one of the Parties (hereinafter the &quot;Disclosing Party&quot;) communicates to the other Party (hereinafter the &quot;Receiving Party&quot;), in whatever form — written, oral, electronic or on any other medium — and in particular: (a) the exchanges between the Customer and FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS, the contents of this Contract and its annexes, and more generally the course of the relationship between the Parties; (b) the Content to which the Customer has access in connection with the Services, including Candidate Content and the information, analyses, studies and data made available by FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS; (c) any information relating to the business, strategy, processes, financial data, clients or staff of the Disclosing Party. By way of exception, information that is freely available to the public at the time of its communication, or that becomes so without any breach of a legal or contractual obligation incumbent on the Receiving Party, and information already known to the Receiving Party — provided it can demonstrate that it obtained access to that information without breaching any such obligations — shall not be considered Confidential Information. By way of exception, FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS may publish anonymous statistics on the use of its Services. </p><p> Each Party undertakes not to disclose any Confidential Information to a third party and to use it in accordance with the purpose of the Services. It shall restrict access to its representatives, employees or agents to what is necessary for them to perform the tasks entrusted to them. It shall apply appropriate measures to protect the confidentiality of such information, at a level at least equal to that which it applies to the protection of its own confidential information. </p><p> This confidentiality clause shall remain in force for a period of 10 years after the end of the Contract, for whatever reason. </p><p> 6.7. Commercial references – Unless it expressly objects in writing, the Customer authorises FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS to cite it among its client references, on its website and on other media, including by reproducing its logo. FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS undertakes not to make any use thereof contrary to standard commercial practice. </p><p> 6.8. Referral programme – Our referral programme allows your users to recommend our platform to third parties and to obtain rewards where a subscription is taken out. By accepting these general terms, you authorise them to take part in our programme. You may withdraw that authorisation at any time by sending a request to users@turnover-it.com. The programme terms may be consulted at: https://app.turnover-it.com/referral-conditions </p><p> 6.9. Personal data – FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS undertakes to comply with the personal data protection legislation applicable in France, and in particular Regulation (EU) No 2016/679, known as the &quot;General Data Protection Regulation&quot; (hereinafter &quot;GDPR&quot;), and French Act No. 78-17 of 6 January 1978 on Information Technology, Data Files and Civil Liberties. It is the Customer&#39;s responsibility to check whether its use of the Services is compatible with any other legislation, and in particular the national legislation of other European Union Member States. </p><p> FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS is the controller of the personal data processing relating to the compilation and management of the Databases. It alone determines the means and purposes of that processing and alone assumes compliance with the obligations of transparency, of collecting consent (or offering an opt-out) and of responding to requests to exercise data subject rights. The Customer is informed that the CV Database is compiled on the basis of consent, the limits of which are reflected in our Terms of Use. The Customer acts as an independent controller when it consults the personal data in the Databases. </p><p> The Customer acts as controller and FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS as processor for the processing carried out by means of the tools made available by FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS to carry out or facilitate recruitment, and in particular the ATS software. Such processing activities are governed by the Data Processing Agreement set out in the Annex (the &quot;DPA&quot;). </p><p> 6.10. Restrictive interpretation – The authorisations granted to the Customer must be construed strictly and are limited to those expressly provided for. </p><h4>7. Force majeure, Liability, Warranties</h4><p> 7.1. Force majeure – For the purposes of the Contract, events of force majeure include any event beyond the control of and/or independent of the will of FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS, such as, without limitation, natural disaster, strikes, frost, fire, storm, flood, epidemic, supply difficulties, strike or other labour dispute, malfunction or interruption of national or international communication channels affecting its service(s), by reason of its unforeseeable and irresistible nature. In all cases of force majeure, FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS is released from all liability, whether in contract or in tort, under any warranty or on any other basis, for any loss caused directly or indirectly by the force majeure event, and is consequently liable for no damages or compensation whatsoever for the total or partial non-performance of its obligations. In the first instance, the force majeure event referred to above suspends performance of the contract; if the force majeure event lasts more than two (2) months, either party may terminate the contract by registered letter with acknowledgement of receipt. </p><p> 7.2. Best-efforts obligations – All obligations incumbent on FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS constitute best-efforts obligations (obligations de moyens). </p><p> 7.3. Exclusion of liability – FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS may not be held liable: </p><ul><li> to the fullest extent permitted by law, for the consequences of the conduct or content of Candidates, other Customers or third parties. FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS is under no general obligation to monitor, without prejudice to its right to carry out checks to verify compliance with its contractual terms; </li><li> as regards security, it is recalled that it is bound by a best-efforts obligation. FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS cannot protect the Customer against malicious uses of its Services. In particular, since the CV Database offers Candidates&#39; original CVs, we cannot guarantee 100% that they are free from viruses or malware. FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS may not be held liable for the consequences of downloading and opening a CV in Word or PDF format containing viruses, macros or any other type of malware; </li><li> the Services are made available as is, with any imperfections they may contain, which the Customer expressly accepts. The Customer acknowledges that the Services may contain imperfections, anomalies and errors inherent in any software. </li></ul><p> Furthermore, FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS may not incur liability in respect of the consequences of: </p><ul><li> the temporary or permanent loss, alteration or unavailability of data; </li><li> the quality, accuracy, completeness or reliability of the Site or its Content, and in particular Content published on the blog, the newsletter and other