 damage was discovered or from the day it ought to have been known. The expiry of this period entails the forfeiture of any right to claim compensation in money or in kind from FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS, including the performance of any obligation to act. </p><p> 7.7. Enforceability against third parties – To the fullest extent permitted by law, these limitations of liability of FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS are enforceable against third parties. </p><p> 7.8. Warranties given by FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS – FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS warrants (1) that it holds all rights, authorisations and licences necessary to grant the licence provided for in respect of the FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS Content and (2) that its CV Database has been compiled in compliance with the personal data protection legislation applicable in France, for the purposes provided for in the Contract. In the event of a third-party claim or proceedings initiated by an administrative or judicial authority, FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS shall indemnify the Customer for any loss resulting from a breach of these warranties, in proportion to its fault. This indemnification covers the reasonable defence costs incurred by the Customer for its defence, including lawyers&#39; or experts&#39; fees. </p><p> 7.9. Warranties given by the Customer – The Customer indemnifies FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS on the same terms against all consequences, and in particular all third-party claims or legal actions, prosecutions or inspections by a judicial or administrative authority, arising from (a) its use of the Services in breach of the Contract or not in compliance with applicable law, (b) its use of the Services in breach of third-party rights (in particular intellectual property rights), (c) the unsuitability of the Services selected for its needs, (d) the loss of credentials or the unauthorised use of its access, and (e) the loss of third-party data. In the event of a third-party claim or proceedings initiated by an administrative or judicial authority, the Customer shall indemnify FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS for any loss resulting from a breach of these warranties, in proportion to its fault. This indemnification covers the reasonable defence costs incurred by FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS for its defence, including lawyers&#39; or experts&#39; fees. </p><h4>8. Breach of contractual provisions</h4><p> 8.1. Termination for cause – Either Party may terminate the Contract in the event of a sufficiently serious breach by the other Party. Except in cases of emergency, termination takes effect automatically thirty (30) days after a formal notice has been sent by registered letter with acknowledgement of receipt to the defaulting Party, setting out the breaches alleged and warning it that, failing cessation of the conduct complained of within the aforementioned period, the Contract will be terminated. FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS may terminate the Contract as of right in the event of a breach of the provisions of the Contract relating to intellectual property, confidentiality or personal data, or of a breach of its General Terms and Conditions of Access and Use or of applicable law, in particular as regards the content of advertisements. </p><p> 8.2. Suspension – In the event of a breach of these terms, FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS may slow down, restrict or suspend access to the Services, without prior notice or formal notice. These measures may be implemented during the thirty-day period provided for in the preceding article, “Termination for cause”. </p><h4>9. Miscellaneous</h4><p> 9.1. Changes in legislation – These General Terms and Conditions and the Services may be modified at any time if required by a change in regulations. </p><p> 9.2. Subcontracting – FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS is authorised to subcontract part of the Services. </p><p> 9.3. Independence – It is expressly agreed between the Parties that each acts, for the performance of the Services, in its own name and on its own behalf, as an independent contractor. </p><p> 9.4. Entire agreement – This Contract constitutes the entire commitment of the Parties, no prior writing or exchange being capable of creating any obligation or right on their part. </p><p> 9.5. No waiver – The failure of either Party to rely on any provision of the Contract may not be construed as a waiver of its right subsequently to enforce that provision. </p><p> 9.6. Partial invalidity – Should any provision of this Contract be held invalid under a rule of law in force or a final court decision, it shall be deemed unwritten, without rendering the remainder of the Contract invalid or affecting the validity of its other provisions. The Parties undertake to negotiate in good faith the provisions necessary to replace the invalid clauses. </p><h4>10. Governing law, Jurisdiction</h4><p> 10.1. Governing law – The Contract is governed by French law, to the exclusion of any other legislation, standards or practices, including those of international trade. </p><p> 10.2. Jurisdiction – The courts of Nanterre having subject-matter jurisdiction shall have exclusive jurisdiction over disputes falling within the scope of the Contract, for all proceedings including protective, urgent, warranty-claim and ex parte proceedings, including where there are multiple defendants. </p><h3>II. Terms of Use</h3><h4>11. Terms of Use applicable to all Services</h4><p> 11.1. Intended purpose of the Services – The Customer undertakes to use the Services solely for the purposes of recruiting for a position open within its own company or group, for placing its own consultants between assignments, or for placing such consultants within its own company/group. </p><p> 11.2. Compliance with contractual and technical restrictions – The Customer undertakes to comply with the limits of its access plan and shall refrain from circumventing any technical restrictions put in place by FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS. </p><p> 11.3. Reasonable use – The Customer undertakes to use the Services in a reasonable and considered manner. </p><p> 11.4. Relations with Candidates and other Customers – To the fullest extent permitted by law, FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS is in no way responsible for the relations between the Customer and the other users of the platform. The tools are made available to them and they are fully responsible for the use they make of them, without prejudice to the right of FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS to take measures in the event of a breach of these General Terms and Conditions of Access and Use. In particular, the Customer is responsible for its recruitment processes and for the processing of the personal data of Candidates and other Customers. </p><p> 11.5. Prohibited conduct – The Customer shall refrain from any abusive or unlawful conduct, or any conduct prejudicial to the rights, image or reputation of FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS, a Candidate, another Customer or a third party. </p><p> 11.6. Reporting – The Customer shall report any content or conduct it considers unlawful, abusive or contrary to our contractual terms by email to: users@turnover-it.com. In its message it shall state its identity, the information needed to identify the content (e.g. URL, screenshot) and, if it considers content to be unlawful, a sufficiently substantiated explanation. The term &quot;unlawful content&quot; covers any information which, in itself or in its context, infringes applicable legislation. </p><p> 11.7. Prohibition on extracting the Databases – The Customer is prohibited from extracting and reproducing all or part of the Databases, by any means whatsoever, in particular to build a database of business contacts or to develop a product. </p><p> 11.8. CV Database – Our CV Database is made up of Candidates who have agreed to join it in order to be contacted by recruiters wishing to offer them a position. The Customer is required to obtain their consent independently and by its own means for any other use of their data. Accordingly, it is authorised to (1) access and consult the data in the CV Database, (2) contact Candidates to offer them a position, and (3) ask for their consent to the use of their data for other purposes, which must remain recruitment-related (e.g. joining the Customer&#39;s own CV Database). In particular, the Customer may not use the data to build its own CV Database without obtaining a valid consent. These provisions are supplemented by specific provisions depending on the means of access (Site or API). </p><p> 11.9. Prohibition on sharing with third parties – The Customer shall refrain from communicating to third parties the Content published on the Site or contained in the Databases, and in particular CVs or job offers. </p><p> 11.10. Prohibition on re-use of Content and on secondary uses – The Content to which the Services give access, and in particular the Databases, may not be used for other purposes, and in particular for the training, testing or improvement of artificial intelligence systems, language models or any algorithmic tool, for the development or marketing of services or products, or for benchmarking. These restrictions do not apply where (a) the Customer obtains the Candidates&#39; direct consent to such uses or (b) in the context of recruitment processes, which take place under the Customer&#39;s sole responsibility. </p><p>11.11. Publishing of job offers</p><p> a. Location of the position – The Customer is authorised to publish job offers for positions to be filled anywhere in the world, subject to compliance with applicable legislation and with the obligations set out in the following paragraph. </p><p> b. Content of advertisements – The Customer undertakes to comply with the legislation applicable to the publication of job offers. The following rules are set out as a reminder, this list being non-exhaustive: </p><ul><li> offers relating to positions to be filled on French territory must be drafted in French. They may, however, be accompanied by a translation into another language; </li><li> any discriminatory requirement based on sex, age, origin, family situation, physical appearance, state of health, opinions, or any other prohibited criterion is strictly forbidden; </li><li>the offer must correspond to a genuine recruitment need;</li><li> the content of the offer must be accurate, not misleading, and compliant with the applicable rules of employment law (type of contract, working hours, level of remuneration, etc.); </li><li> it is prohibited to make an application conditional on a payment, on the production of a criminal record extract (save where legally permitted), or on holding a driving licence (save where genuinely necessary for the position); </li><li> access to the job offer and the recruitment process must be free of charge for candidates, without redirecting to paid services or premium-rate numbers; </li><li> the Customer must state the identity of the recruiter in the advertisement or, in the case of an anonymous offer, provide FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS with that recruiter&#39;s name or corporate name and address; </li><li> the Customer must check that its advertisement does not contain any prohibited wording before publishing it. It is invited to consult the many guides available on the subject. </li></ul><p> To the fullest extent permitted by law, the Customer indemnifies FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS against any judicial, extrajudicial or amicable proceedings in the event of a breach of this article, compensating it for all related expenses, including expert and advisory fees. </p><p> The Customer is informed that FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS implements automated means of detecting this type of content. No measure will be taken against the Customer without human intervention. </p><p> c. Dedicated spaces – The Customer undertakes not to publish job offers outside the interface provided for that purpose. For obvious reasons of content organisation and editorial quality, it is in particular prohibited to divert the use of the directory listing by publishing one or more job offers in the &quot;Presentation&quot; area of its company profile. </p><p> 11.12. Forums – The free-work.com website includes forums on which Candidates express themselves freely. FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS does not monitor the statements made, which are the sole responsibility of their authors. It will, however, promptly remove any manifestly unlawful content reported to it. </p><p> 11.13. Contacting candidates – The Customer shall send a reasonable number of communications to Candidates. It shall refrain from any mass or repeated mailing, and shall contact a Candidate only after having fully reviewed their CV. The Customer is informed that Candidates may report spam received to us. In connection with this undertaking, FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS reserves the right to verify usage points and access codes. </p><p> 11.14. Accounts – The number of accounts is limited to one active main account per Customer. The number of associated sub-accounts is limited to 15. Each account is attached to one user. </p><p> 11.15. Credentials – The Customer will receive a username and a password for each main account and sub-account. These credentials are personal to each user. The Customer shall implement appropriate measures to ensure the confidentiality of these credentials. It shall change its password regularly and whenever a member of its team who knows its credentials leaves. </p><p> 11.16. Security – The Customer shall implement appropriate security measures to prevent any unauthorised access to the Services. It shall notify FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS of any unauthorised access within 24 hours of discovering it, providing, as and when available, the information FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS may request, in particular in order to identify the access and the data exposed, assess the resulting risks and ascertain the remediation measures implemented by the Customer. </p><p> 11.17. Breach of the Terms of Use – In the event of a breach of the Terms of Use, FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS may restrict access to the Services or terminate the Contract for the Customer&#39;s breach. FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS may monitor compliance with these terms, including by automated means. </p><h4>12. Additional Terms specific to the use of the Site</h4><p> 12.1. Compatible equipment – The Site is designed to work with the latest versions of the following browsers: Chrome, Firefox, Edge and Safari. We give no warranty of proper operation for use of the site through other browsers, versions other than the latest, or mobile devices such as touchscreen tablets or phones. The Services are provided on an &quot;as is&quot; basis, which the Customer expressly accepts. </p><p> 12.2. Limited CV views – For the purposes of this clause, &quot;viewing a CV&quot; means accessing the content of a CV by clicking on its title, downloading the attachment or hovering over the preview icon. &quot;Viewing a CV&quot; may be carried out, among other ways, from the &quot;CV Database&quot; tab, from the email alert, or from the responses received to a job offer. A &quot;rolling 30-day period&quot; means the last thirty days of use, including the reference day. </p><p> Each access plan includes a maximum number of &quot;CV views&quot; per day and per &quot;rolling 30-day period&quot;, as specified in the quotation and the order form. </p><p> CV views on the platform (excluding CV downloads or any other export via API, webhook or integrations) arising from applications less than 90 days old, as from the date of application, are not deducted from this maximum number and are offered to the Customer. </p><p> The number of CV views is calculated taking into account CV views by all accounts and sub-accounts. </p><p> A number of actual views below the cap gives no right to a refund or to a carry-over to the following period. </p><p> 12.3. Prohibition of automated means – The Customer shall refrain from using, directly or indirectly, any automated process for accessing or interacting with the Site and its Databases, in particular by means of scripts, bots, scrapers, crawlers or any other tool or program intended to extract, query, copy, collect or interact with the platform&#39;s data or features, without the prior written authorisation of FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS. We reserve the right to slow down, restrict or suspend access to the Services if we can reasonably suspect that you are making abusive or fraudulent use of them. </p><p> 12.4. Restrictions on mailings to Candidates – In order to avoid any SPAM in the context of a mailing sent from the CV Database tab, the Customer undertakes to check that the targeted candidate&#39;s profile matches its offer by reviewing the CV in full. If the targeted CV has not been viewed, we reserve the right not to send the mailing. Each candidate targeted by a mailing counts as one full view of their CV. </p><h4>13. Additional Terms specific to the use of the APIs</h4><p> 13.1. Credits – For each access plan including access to an API, the Customer has a number of credits included, which it spends as it uses the API. Credits not used by the end of the access period give rise to no refund. </p><p> 13.2. API key – FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS will provide the Customer with an API key and the documentation required to install the APIs, which the Customer undertakes to comply with and may not disclose to third parties. </p><p> 13.3. Access to the CV Database – The Customer undertakes to comply with the following terms: </p><ul><li> the sole purpose of any request made to the API must be the search for candidates for an open position; </li><li> the Customer is authorised to store the data and process it by means of its own tools designed to facilitate its recruitment, such as its application-tracking software or its matching and scoring tools, under its sole responsibility; </li><li> unless valid Candidate consent has been obtained independently by the Customer, storage of their data may not go beyond the scope of the recruitment for the position for which that data was obtained. The Customer may therefore not retain it for future recruitment. </li></ul><h4>14. Additional Terms specific to Recruitment Agency Customers</h4><p> 14.1. The Recruitment Agency Customer is authorised to use the Services to contribute to a recruitment for a position open at one of its clients and to communicate Candidates&#39; data to them for that purpose. </p><p>14.2. The Recruitment Agency Customer undertakes not to:</p><ul><li> communicate all or part of the Candidate data from the CV Database to third parties otherwise than in the case provided for in the preceding paragraph; </li><li> make all or part of the Candidate data accessible to the public or to a restricted audience, such as its own clients via its platform, its websites, its newsletter or by any other means or medium; </li><li> send a Candidate any communication for purposes other than recruitment for an open position. </li></ul><h3>Annex: Data Processing Agreement (&quot;DPA&quot;)</h3><p> This agreement (the &quot;Agreement&quot;) sets out the terms and conditions under which the Customer entrusts FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS, within the framework of the Contract, with carrying out the personal data processing described in its Annex I &quot;Description of the processing”. </p><p> This processing is carried out in the name and on behalf of the Customer, which acts as Controller, FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS acting as Processor within the meaning of the GDPR. </p><p> The Agreement, including Annexes I and II thereto, forms an integral part of the Contract. The other provisions of the Contract apply to it, including those governing liability and jurisdiction. In the event of any conflict between the Agreement and those provisions, the Agreement prevails. </p><h4>Definitions and interpretation</h4><p> The Agreement must be read and interpreted in the light of the provisions of the GDPR. Where terms of the Agreement are defined in the Contract or in the GDPR, they shall have the meaning so given. </p><p>The following terms are defined as follows:</p><ul><li> &quot;Supervisory Authority&quot; means the Commission Nationale de l&#39;Informatique et des Libertés (&quot;CNIL&quot;), without prejudice to any mandatory provisions liable to confer jurisdiction on another administrative authority. </li><li> &quot;Description of the processing&quot; means Annex I to the Agreement, describing the personal data processing entrusted under the data processing arrangements governed by this Agreement. </li><li> &quot;Personal data&quot; means personal data within the meaning of Article 4 of the GDPR. </li><li> &quot;Applicable Regulations&quot; means any regulations on the protection of Personal data applicable to the processing governed by the Agreement, and by default any regulations in that field applicable to the processing governed by the Contract. </li><li>&quot;Controller&quot; means the Customer.</li><li> &quot;GDPR&quot; means Regulation (EU) 2016/679 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 27 April 2016 on the protection of natural persons with regard to the processing of personal data and on the free movement of such data, together with the implementing standards and recommendations issued by the bodies and institutions of the European Union and by the CNIL, as well as its interpretation in the case law of the Court of Justice and of the French courts. </li><li>&quot;Processor&quot; means FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS.</li><li> &quot;Personal data breach&quot; means a breach of security leading to the accidental or unlawful destruction, loss, alteration, unauthorised disclosure of, or access to, personal data transmitted, stored or otherwise processed. </li></ul><h4>Description of the processing, duration</h4><p> The processing governed by the Agreement is defined in Annex I &quot;Description of the processing&quot;, as is the retention period for the personal data. </p><h4>Obligations of the Processor</h4><h5>Instructions</h5><p> The Processor shall process Personal data only on documented instructions from the Controller, unless required to do so by Union or Member State law to which it is subject. In that case, the Processor shall inform the Controller of that legal requirement before processing, unless the law prohibits it from doing so on important grounds of public interest. The Contract and Annex I to the Agreement &quot;Description of the processing&quot; are deemed to contain the initial instructions. </p><p> It is for the Controller to ensure that its instructions comply with the Applicable Regulations on data protection, the Processor bearing no liability in that respect. </p><h5>Limitation of purposes</h5><p> The Processor shall process Personal data solely for the specific purpose or purposes of the processing, as defined in Annex I to the Agreement &quot;Description of the processing”. </p><h5>Security of processing</h5><p> The Processor shall implement appropriate technical and organisational measures to ensure the security and confidentiality of Personal data in the light of the resources available to it. In assessing the appropriate level of security, it shall take due account of the state of the art, the costs of implementation and the nature, scope, context and purposes of the processing, as well as the risks to data subjects. </p><p> The Processor warrants that it limits access to personal data by its staff to what is necessary for the performance of the Contract and ensures that they are bound by a contractual or statutory obligation of confidentiality. </p><h5>Compliance</h5><p> At the Controller&#39;s request, the Processor shall provide it with the information necessary to demonstrate compliance with the obligations incumbent on it under the Agreement. </p><p> The Controller may carry out, at its own expense, an audit to assess the Processor&#39;s compliance with this Agreement, conducted by an independent auditor approved in advance by the Processor. Each audit must be at least twelve months apart from the previous one. In the case of an on-site audit, the Processor shall grant access to its premises between 10:00 and 18:00 on business days. Any audit must be preceded by 30 calendar days&#39; notice, the Processor having 10 days to object to the auditor appointed. The Controller shall send the draft final report and shall have 30 days to submit its observations, which must be incorporated into the final report. The audit must be conducted taking into account the Processor&#39;s operational and organisational constraints and ensuring that the resources mobilised and the duration of the audit operations remain reasonable and proportionate. </p><p> The Processor shall assist the Controller in fulfilling its obligations regarding impact assessments and consultation of the supervisory authority. Its involvement will be invoiced to the Controller. </p><p> It shall also implement the measures necessary to enable the Controller to respond to requests from data subjects to exercise their rights. </p><p> Where it becomes aware of a Personal data breach covered by the Agreement, the Processor shall inform the Controller as soon as possible. It shall provide it with the following information, in two communications if necessary: </p><ul><li> the nature of the Personal data, including, where possible, the categories and approximate number of data subjects concerned by the breach and the categories and approximate number of Personal data records concerned; </li><li>any measures it has taken or plans to take to address the breach;</li><li> the relevant information in its possession likely to assist the Controller in assessing the likely consequences of the Personal data breach. </li></ul><h4>Use of sub-processors</h4><p> The Processor has general authorisation to engage sub-processors. The sub-processors existing at the time of the Agreement are listed in Annex II to the Agreement. </p><p> It shall engage only sub-processors offering sufficient guarantees of compliance with privacy protection Regulations. </p><p> The Processor shall specifically inform the Controller in writing of any intended change to this list through the addition or replacement of sub-processors. The Controller has seven (7) days from receipt of that information to object to the new sub-processor. In the event of a reasoned and reasonable objection, the Processor may not proceed with the intended engagement. It is for the Controller to provide an email address for receiving sub-processor updates. </p><p> The Processor shall impose by contract on the sub-processor data protection obligations equivalent to those imposed on the Processor by the Agreement. </p><h4>International transfers</h4><p> The Processor may transfer Personal data outside the European Economic Area (EEA), provided it implements the measures necessary to ensure that the transfer does not result in a breach of Chapter V of the GDPR. </p><h4>Suspension, End of the Agreement</h4><p> In the event of a breach by the Processor of the obligations incumbent on it under the Agreement or under privacy protection Regulations, the Controller may instruct the Processor to suspend the processing of Personal data until the Processor complies with the Agreement or the Contract is terminated in accordance with the applicable provisions. </p><p> Following the end of the Agreement, for whatever reason, the Processor shall, at the Controller&#39;s option, delete all Personal data processed on the Controller&#39;s behalf. On request, it shall also provide the Controller with a copy of that data. This service will be invoiced by the Processor to the Controller. </p><h4>Governing law, Disputes and Competent supervisory authority</h4><p> The Agreement is fully subject to the provisions of the Contract relating to governing law, disputes and competent courts. </p><p> Save where mandatory provisions provide otherwise, the Commission Nationale de l&#39;Informatique et des Libertés has sole jurisdiction over the processing governed by the Agreement, including in the event of transfers of Personal data outside France. </p><h4>Annex I: Description of the processing</h4><p>1. Categories of data subjects:</p><ul><li>Candidates</li><li> Consultants between assignments, employees or representatives of other Customers </li></ul><p>2. Purposes:</p><ul><li> Recruitment of Candidates, placement of consultants between assignments </li><li> ATS system: receipt of applications, management of recruitment processes, messaging </li><li> Sourcing: optimized candidate search and ranking tools. The Processor shall communicate to the Controller, on request and upon any substantial change, a description of the artificial-intelligence matching features, comprising: the categories of data used, the main ranking criteria, the provider of the model where it constitutes a sub-processor within the meaning of the GDPR, and the measures implemented to prevent and test bias. The matching results constitute an aid to decision-making and do not give rise to any decision based solely on automated processing, the final decision belonging to the Controller. </li><li>Performance tracking tools</li></ul><p>3. Personal data processed:</p><ul><li> Candidate profile: identity, address, occupation, CV, objectives and availability, access to soft skills assessments </li><li>Candidates&#39; contact details</li><li>Personal data exchanged via the communication tools</li></ul><p>4. Retention period:</p><ul><li>For the term of the Contract</li></ul><h4>Annex II: List of sub-processors</h4><table><thead><tr><th>Sub-processor</th><th>Purposes of sub-processing</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Amazon Web Services (AWS)</td><td>Hosting and backup provider</td></tr><tr><td>HrFlow.ai</td><td>CV and job-offer parsing provider</td></tr><tr><td>Mailjet (Sinch)</td><td>Emailing provider</td></tr><tr><td>AssessFirst</td><td>Soft skills assessment provider</td></tr><tr><td>HoptyCV</td><td>Skills-dossier generation provider</td></tr></tbody></table>`,180)]))}};t();var c={class:`p-3 lg:p-6 prose prose-sm max-w-full`},l={key:0},u={__name:`TermsOfService`,props:{hasHeading:{type:Boolean,default:!1}},setup(t){return(a,o)=>(i(),e(`div`,c,[t.hasHeading?(i(),e(`h2`,l,` CONDITIONS GÉNÉRALES D’ACCÈS ET D’UTILISATION DES SERVICES `)):n(``,!0),o[0]||=r(`<p>Dernière modification : 28/10/2026</p><p> Le site turnover-it.com (ci-après le “Site”) et les services qu’il propose (ci-après les “Services”) sont fournis par la société FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS, au capital de 50 000 euros, dont le siège social est situé 35 rue de Paris, 92100 Boulogne-Billancourt, immatriculée au registre du commerce et des sociétés de Nanterre sous le numéro 450 955 893, (ci-après ”FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS&quot; ou “nous”). </p><p> Les Services sont fournis soumis aux conditions contractuelles suivantes, que le client (ci-après le “Client” ou “vous”) accepte sans réserve : </p><ul><li>Conditions générales d’accès ;</li><li>Conditions générales d’utilisation ;</li><li>Conditions relatives à certains services ;</li><li>Accord de sous-traitance de données personnelles ;</li><li>Bon de commande (édité en dernière étape de souscription).</li></ul><p> Ces documents forment l’intégralité de l’accord des parties (ci-après le “Contrat”), à l’exclusion de tout autre accord précédent entre les parties et de la documentation contractuelle du Client telle que ses éventuelles conditions générales d’achat. En cas de contradiction ou incohérence, il sera fait application du document le plus bas dans cette liste. </p><h3>I. Conditions générales d’accès</h3><h4>1. Définitions</h4><p> “Base de données” désigne tout ensemble structuré de données constitué par FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS. Les Bases de données font partie du Contenu FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS. </p><p>“Candidat” désigne un membre inscrit sur le site free-work.com.</p><p> “Client Cabinet de recrutement” désigne les Clients souscrivant à un accès et ayant pour activité la prise en charge totale ou partielle de processus de recrutements de leurs clients. </p><p> “Contenu” désigne l&#39;ensemble des données, informations, documents, fichiers, textes, images, vidéos, enregistrements audio ou audiovisuels, graphiques, métadonnées, bases de données, modèles, formulaires, questionnaires, rapports, analyses, recommandations, bonnes pratiques, méthodologies, procédés, codes sources, codes objets et exécutables, documentation, matériel de conception préparatoire, interfaces, logotypes, dessins, designs auxquels le Client est susceptible d’accéder dans le cadre des Services. </p><p> “Contenu FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS” désigne le Contenu appartenant ou licencié à FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS. </p><p> “Contenu des candidats” désigne le Contenu communiqué ou publié par les Candidats. </p><p> “Contenu des autres Clients et tiers” désigne le Contenu communiqué ou publié par les autres Clients et d’éventuels tiers. </p><h4>2. Objet</h4><p>Les présentes Conditions générales prévoient :</p><ul><li> Les conditions dans lesquelles FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS fournit les Services au Client ; </li><li> Les conditions applicables aux différents accès auxquels le Client peut souscrire ; </li><li>Les règles qu’il doit respecter lorsqu’il utilise les Services.</li></ul><h4>3. Services proposés</h4><p>Notre plateforme propose notamment les Services suivant :</p><ul><li> L’accès à notre CVthèque constituée de Candidats membres de notre site free-work.com ; </li><li> La publication d’annonces de recherche de Candidats sur free-work.com ; </li><li> L’accès à notre Place de marché B2B, dédiée au recrutement de consultants en intercontrat, qui permet d’accéder aux appels d’offres, de publier vos profils et nouer des partenariats ; </li><li> Un logiciel de recrutement fourni en Saas (Applicant Tracking Systems, “ATS”) ; </li><li> Des outils pour améliorer et accélérer vos recrutements, tels que le matching IA et des outils de suivi. </li></ul><p> Certains Services peuvent faire l’objet d’intégration dans le système du Client grâce à nos API. </p><p> Dans le cadre de notre politique d&#39;amélioration continue ou pour des raisons commerciales, nous nous réservons le droit de faire évoluer nos Services en cours de contrat, y compris par l&#39;ajout ou la suppression de fonctionnalités. Ces évolutions ne sauraient toutefois remettre en cause les fonctionnalités essentielles incluses dans l&#39;accès souscrit. Toute nouvelle fonctionnalité impliquant un traitement de données personnelles, notamment par intelligence artificielle, fera l&#39;objet d&#39;une information écrite préalable du Client avant sa mise en œuvre. </p><h4>4. Souscription d’un accès</h4><p> 4.1. Personnes éligibles - L’accès à nos Services est réservé aux personnes morales dûment enregistrés comme telles et disposant d’un numéro SIRET ou d’un numéro d’immatriculation d’entreprise équivalent. </p><p> 4.2. Pouvoir - Le Client garantit que la personne opérant la souscription est dûment habilitée en ce sens. </p><p> 4.3. Sélection de l’accès - Le Client choisit la formule d’accès qui lui convient, dont la dernière étape avant règlement est l’émission d’un bon de commande rappelant le contenu de la formule choisie. Le Client pourra faire évoluer son accès vers une formule supérieure à tout moment, mais ne dispose pas de droit de rétrograder son accès à une formule inférieure en cours de contrat. </p><p> 4.4. Responsabilité du Client - Il appartient au Client de s’assurer avant de confirmer sa commande par un règlement que les Services proposés correspondent à ses besoins et que l’utilisation qu’il envisage des Services est conforme à nos conditions contractuelles et à toute réglementation applicable. Les Services sont fournis tels quels. </p><p> 4.5. Souscription définitive - La souscription est définitive et irréversible à la réception du règlement par FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS, sans droit de rétractation. L’accès aux Services sera fourni par la durée de l’accès souscrit, sans droit de résiliation avant son terme ou droit à remboursement pour quelque raison que ce soit. </p><p> 4.6. Essai - Les périodes d’essai sont pleinement soumises aux présentes Conditions générales. La période d’essai court que les Services soient effectivement utilisés ou non. Nous pouvons mettre fin à l’essai à tout moment, sans avoir à fournir de motif. </p><h4>5. Durée et conditions financières</h4><h5>5.1. Conditions applicables à tous les accès</h5><p> 5.1.1. Prix - Les tarifs en vigueur et prix sont exprimés en euros hors taxes, FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS se réservant le droit de reporter toute nouvelle taxe ou évolution d’une taxe existante. </p><p> Dans le cas où le Client serait tenu d’effectuer une retenue sur ses paiements, il devra majorer ses paiements de sorte à ce que FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS reçoive le montant net qui lui aurait été versé en l’absence de toute retenue. </p><p> 5.1.2. Remises - Pour des périodes limitées, FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS peut proposer des remises, sans droit du Client au maintien de ces offres. </p><p> 5.1.3. Absence d’escompte - Aucun escompte ne sera appliqué pour un règlement anticipé. </p><p> 5.1.4. Evolution des prix - FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS se réserve le droit de faire évoluer librement les prix des accès, sans que le client n’ait droit au maintien d’un prix d’une souscription à l’autre. </p><h5>5.2. Conditions spécifiques aux accès à durée fixe</h5><p> 5.2.1. Durée - Les accès souscrits pour une durée fixe sont conclus sans renouvellement tacite. Le Client est engagé jusqu’au terme et ne bénéficie d’aucun droit à remboursement ou à une résiliation anticipée. </p><p> 5.2.2. Règlement et début de l’accès - Le paiement a lieu par carte bancaire ou virement bancaire. En cas de paiement par virement, l’accès ne débute qu&#39;à compter de la bonne réception du règlement et du traitement de la commande par FREE-WORK / AGSI SAS. </p><p> 5.2.3. Période de gel - Lorsque la formule souscrite inclut la fonctionnalité de gel, telle qu’indiquée au bon de commande, le Client dispose de 6 périodes de 7 jours consécutifs (une &quot;Période de gel&quot;) à répartir sur la du